(B/'CHANGELOG-v1.20.md').write_text('# v1.20 changes\n\nSuccessor of the accepted v1.19 authority (5efbcae6, manifest 06811f07b422d1cdf30ae6c076bae2bc0b598fc3ac464a0e180a8553a76a2848; human acceptance recorded 2026-09-20). Adds the independently freeze-review-approved Resolve Control Plane Phase 1 as the accepted READ-ONLY control substrate (implementation 77c26103, pinned in PHASE1-SOURCE-PIN.json; qualification carried forward by identity in PHASE1-QUALIFICATION-RECORD.json), binds the qualification-library observations in TARGET-CONTRACT.json, states the protocol-closed semantics of the vendor scripting port, records the 2026-09-20 live multi-client observations, and freezes the bounded P3 items with closure gates (KNOWN-LIMITATIONS-PHASE1.md).\n\nAdded: three-host read-only control plane doctrine (CONTROL-PLANE.md), explicit-target/no-fallback law, per-host local workers, authenticated vrc.v1 protocol, worker/Resolve/project/timeline identity model, qualification-library gate, durable replay protection, saturation observability, bounded session lifetime, structured journaling.\n\nNot added: Hermes integration (facade ABSENT), persistent workers, any Resolve write capability, write lease, production write qualification. WRITE AUTHORITY = NONE. All v1.19 repairs (V118-M1..M4, N1..N3) are retained and regression-tested. Implementation-author candidate; independent review required.\n\nRepair candidate (authority version unchanged, 1.20.0): the first v1.20 candidate e65ed5a4 (manifest 2f58bc3b23693d97e0bda480c0b560ec3ed9eedb375d050b22a1936420f9b6c0) was independently reviewed on 2026-09-21 and REJECTED - REPAIR REQUIRED (review manifest 740c656d1a1c5e261d45a3656922b2aa4bc2e1dbb2901909085e2d7a9b4bc546; P0 0, P1 0, P2 3, P3 5 new + 8 inherited). This candidate repairs the three P2 bundle-construction defects at generator level (F-120-01 parent-pin byte count, F-120-02 manifest rule version, F-120-03 stale inherited v1.19 matrix), closes the validator blind spots that let them pass (F-120-05: sections external-pins, authority-version, inherited-matrices, registered-json), machine-verifies PHASE1-SOURCE-PIN.json against resolve-control/** (phase1-pin) and documents the one-validator-per-host operating constraint (F-120-04). resolve-control/**, v1.18, v1.19, the Phase 1 qualification evidence and the recorded human v1.19 acceptance are unchanged; e65ed5a4 remains in branch history as the rejected candidate. Still an implementation-author candidate; independent re-review required.\n\nFinal repair (authority version unchanged, 1.20.0): the repaired candidate 1e2ce233 (manifest b296dc6a952532994dd99886b3a8158bfecc8b4763191ff83ab4dfc4af2d4638) was independently re-reviewed on 2026-09-21 (review manifest 79923a9bc96040675f4dfd99da460eb6efc5e975a56f86476cc84c180409ecab): F-120-01/02/03 confirmed closed, two P2 blockers found and repaired here - F-120-04 (self-test seam: own-session-only ownership, no whole-tree removal, run-unique ids; section selftest-ownership) and F-120-09 (environment-bound values in the frozen report; environment scrub, outcome-only inventory detail, section report-determinism). Both rejected candidates stay in branch history. Still an implementation-author candidate; independent re-review required.\n')
