(B/'RELEASE-AUTHORITY.md').write_text('# v1.20 release authority\n\nThis is an implementation-author candidate. Exactly one structured Resolve current selector lives in DOC-AUTHORITY.md, and all current normative prose must agree. The current manifest is referenced by path rather than digest there; its external pin binds the final document bytes. The parent is the accepted v1.19 authority (5efbcae6); v1.18 and v1.19 are immutable history.\n\nFinalize registration, generate machine artifacts, verify source-bound reference metadata, publish inventory, build manifest, validate, rebuild manifest, validate again, and require byte equality. A failed check never authorizes a run.\n\nArtifact inclusion is parent-universe plus explicit successor artifacts (CONTROL-PLANE.md, KNOWN-LIMITATIONS-PHASE1.md, LINEAGE.md, PHASE1-SOURCE-PIN.json, PHASE1-QUALIFICATION-RECORD.json), checked against actual membership and registration. Symbol extraction retains explicit module identity; bare references require document context.\n\nRequired validation IDs are frozen separately from the executing check list. Omitting any mandatory check fails exact set parity.\n\nNo receipt, root, workflow, evidence carrier or transaction semantics are changed. No write authority, Hermes integration or operational authorization is implied. WRITE AUTHORITY = NONE.\n\nSelf-test evidence ownership law (F-120-04, v1.20 final repair): a validator run owns exactly one filesystem object under the governed root /home/vidtoolz/resolve-qualification-evidence/attachment - the session directory <root>/<name> for a run-unique, collision-resistant self-test id (sess-selftest-<tag>-<pid>-<128-bit token>) that did not exist at entry - and its cleanup removes exactly that directory (lstat-checked: a real directory, not a symlink, directly under the root) and nothing else: never the root, never a sibling, never the qualification tree, whether or not the root existed before the run and whether the run exits normally or by exception. Root absence at entry grants no ownership of anything that later appears beneath it. If the governed root is absent it is created with the frozen mode and left in place, possibly empty. Pre-existing sessions and sessions created by any other writer during the run survive; an existing name is never adopted. Concurrent validators and other evidence writers therefore need no operating restriction for evidence safety; running validators one at a time remains advisable only for host load. Validation requires the repository checkout with resolve-control/** present (section phase1-pin).\n\nReproducible validation and build contract (F-120-09): the frozen bundle bytes, including VALIDATION-REPORT.md and FREEZE-MANIFEST.json, depend only on the canonical source - never on the checkout location, the working directory, the temp directory (TMPDIR) or its path length, or filesystem device and inode numbers. Every recorded check detail is scrubbed of such values (fixed tokens <TMPDIR>, <REPO>, <CWD>, <SHA256>, inode <N>, sess-selftest-<RUN>), no raw environment-derived total is published, and section report-determinism fails a run that leaks one. Contract for a reviewer: archive the candidate commit anywhere, run the validator alone (python3 -B tools/validate_v1_20.py) and observe zero changed files; run the regeneration cycle (build, prepare, manifest, inventory, manifest, validate, inventory, manifest, validate, manifest - no reference-metadata remap, which is a one-time construction step) and observe changed_files = 0; repeat under a different scratch root and TMPDIR and observe identical bundle hashes and manifest.\n\nRelease-identity law (v1.20 repair, F-120-01/02/03/05/06): every external pin is re-verified by path, sha256 and byte count and every ancestor digest must be pinned; the manifest rule text, the DOC-AUTHORITY selector, TARGET-CONTRACT.json, MILESTONES.md and every release-metadata record must name the same authority version; every inherited finding matrix must equal the accepted parent frozen copy except for its authority_version stamp and the parent matrix must still enumerate the accepted parent findings; every top-level JSON member must validate against the schema it declares or carry an explicit NO_REGISTERED_SCHEMA reason in the manifest; resolve-control/** must equal PHASE1-SOURCE-PIN.json. The manifest build refuses to write when its own pins or version statements fail these laws.\n')

fc=json.loads((B/"AUTHORITY-FUNCTION-CLASSES.json").read_text())
fc["slot_discovery_law"]={'definition': 'Every concrete occurrence of every canonical authority_lib function class is in scope, in JSON keys and values and logical Markdown units. Metadata records are declarations about occurrences, not recursively scanned occurrences. Source-bound declarations cannot suppress contradictory normative predicates.', 'roles': ['AUTHORIZING_DESIGNATION', 'DIAGNOSTIC_DECLARATION', 'HISTORICAL_STATEMENT', 'MENTION', 'AMBIGUOUS_CURRENT_REFERENCE'], 'authority_tokens': ['authoritative', 'authorizing', 'authority', 'refuses', 'refusal', 'refusing', 'decides', 'derived by', 'derives', 'evaluated by', 'enforces', 'governs', 'controls', 'determines', 'adjudicates', 'authorizes', 'blocks', 'permits', 'certifies', 'rejects', 'establishes', 'gates', 'validates', 'loader'], 'class_tokens': ['DIAGNOSTIC', 'diagnostic', 'NON_AUTHORIZING', 'non-authorizing', 'PROVISIONAL_UNTIL_M3'], 'history_tokens': ['formerly', 'historically', 'was then'], 'clause_law': "A claim is read ONLY from the clause containing the reference. Clauses break at '.', ';', ':', ',' and newline, at parenthesis depth zero, and only where the delimiter is followed by whitespace or the end of the text - so an argument list, a dotted module path and a version number stay intact while ordinary punctuation ends a clause. Wrapped markdown prose is rejoined into logical lines first, so where a line happens to wrap cannot change a classification.", 'negation_law': "Negation is LOCAL, never a phrase search. 'X is no longer authoritative; Y is authoritative' classifies X non-authorizing and Y authorizing, because each clause is read separately. No bare negation appears in any token list: the v1.16 scanner exempted any sentence containing the phrase 'no longer', and in the TOCTOU law that phrase modified 'the bundle's binding no longer resolves' - an unrelated clause - which suppressed a real diagnostic-name violation (V116-B1).", 'signal_precedence': ['Schema-defined class keys and registered superseded rows establish structural role.', 'Collect own-clause per-reference predicates independently. Reject a conflicting metadata declaration.', 'Source-bound structured declaration resolves otherwise ambiguous prose; then predicate-local fallback. Unresolved current references fail closed.'], 'reference_forms': ['bare', 'module-qualified', 'anchor (module.py#name)', 'path-qualified (tools/module.py#name)', 'markdown code (`name`)', 'call form name(args)'], 'module_awareness': 'A same-named function in another module is a DIFFERENT symbol: evidence_authoring.derive_attachment_state is the AUTHORIZING authoring wrapper, not the diagnostic authority_lib core function, and is recorded as a foreign-module symbol rather than judged against the authority_lib class map.', 'laws': {'R1': 'A current demoted function reference requires its own non-authorizing declaration or registered historical context; neither may contradict a current authority predicate.', 'R2': 'every clause that designates authority names a function whose canonical class is authorizing'}, 'artifact_scope': 'derived from AUTHORITY-PRECEDENCE.json: status STILL_ACTIVE and role in (NORMATIVE_AUTHORITY, CORRECTION_RECORD). Never a filename pattern. GENERATED_EVIDENCE (the validation report and the generated inventory) reports what the suite checked and quotes its own check names, so it is out of scope by published role; HISTORICAL_INPUT is out of scope by status.', 'generated_inventory': 'AUTHORITY-SLOT-INVENTORY.json', 'generator': 'tools/authority_slots.py, used by both this build and validate_v1_19.py', 'reference_metadata': 'AUTHORITY-REFERENCE-METADATA.json', 'document_universe': 'AUTHORITY-DOCUMENT-UNIVERSE.json', 'ambiguity_law': 'AMBIGUOUS_CURRENT_REFERENCE fails validation; current decision-function MENTION is allowed only for an explicitly foreign module symbol.', 'reference_universe': 'All functions in the canonical authorizing, diagnostic, provisional and internal class arrays; values and JSON keys (location suffix .@key).', 'history_law': 'Registered superseded statement rows use their frozen effective version in both JSON and Markdown. A free-text historical annotation cannot erase a current authority predicate.'}
fc["slot_discovery_law"]["non_authorizing_occurrences"]="DIAGNOSTIC_DECLARATION records a non-authorizing occurrence, including internal helper descriptions and data identifiers sharing function names. It does not demote the canonical function class. An independently detected authority predicate cannot be suppressed by that declaration."
dump("AUTHORITY-FUNCTION-CLASSES.json",fc)
